From: Luissalet <luismasc16@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 01:11:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/36] Iterate puts back what was typed, not what was sent

The resolved prompt cannot be re-entered into the composer: by the time it
is written down, @Elena has already become her trigger word and her
description, so generating from that text would apply neither the LoRA nor
the portrait a second time. The recipe now carries the three slots as the
writer typed them, and older rows fall back to the prompt as before.

The reference editor's text fields are debounced too. They were writing to
Dexie and reloading the whole cast on every keystroke, which is the exact
shape of the dropped-character bug useDebouncedField was written for.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
